  "notes_for_annotators": "Inputs are numbered from 0. One encounter, a tavern brawl from input 7, against two drunks. The merchant is in the encounter but neutral: under the engine's NPC policy he has no opponents, so he Dodges on every turn and never attacks, and nobody attacks him. Narration of the merchant joining the fight, or being hurt, is a CONTRADICT divergence. Cure Wounds on the unhurt merchant at input 14 heals nothing (he is at full hit points) but still spends one of Hollis's two slots, so narration of it mending his wounds is a CONTRADICT divergence, and the cast at input 25 spends the last slot. Input 15 is a narration-only turn that invites a hit-point band phrase about Hollis. The ale is gained at input 6 and drunk at input 16; the room key stays in the inventory, so unlocking the room at input 24 is consistent. The stranger goes down from unfriendly to hostile at input 5 and back up at input 21, so his reply at input 22 should be cool rather than warm; Bess goes up twice to allied. Input 23 asks about coin, and there is no currency in the game. Inputs 7 to 13 give more attacks than the fight usually needs; extra ones are rejected and do not advance the game."
